WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:07.589
A placebo is a treatment with zero
therapeutic value but magical healing

00:00:07.589 --> 00:00:13.160
power. Common placebos include sugar
pills inert saline injections, other

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:18.510
procedures and surgeries that are
completely fake. Placebos are especially

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:24.420
effective to treat pain, chronic stress
related diseases, like insomnia, and forms

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:29.849
of depression. What most don't realize is
that while placebos are fake the placebo

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:36.350
effect does it's magic even if you get
real treatments from a normal doctor.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:42.360
Placebos tend to follow one simple rule:
the more ritualized and extreme the fake

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:47.969
treatment the more effective their
effect. In short, sugar pills work well,

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:53.610
sham surgery works wonders. Since
standard doctor appointments are often

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:59.280
highly ritualized the placebo effect is
part of the cure we think we receive. To

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.530
understand this better let's look at Mr.
and Mrs. Martin who both suffer chronic

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:11.760
back pain. Mr. Martin feels the pain
first and he decides to go see a doctor

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:18.299
who diagnoses osteoporosis and treats
him with physiotherapy. After a few days

00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:23.850
of treatment, Mr. Martin feels better. He
starts to track the progress of his pain.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:28.500
He soon learns that he always goes to
the doctor on the days when the pain is

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:34.130
the worst and always feels better soon
after. He becomes a big advocate for

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:39.390
physiotherapy and recommends it to his
wife and she joins him. But do we really

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:46.680
know that the therapy works? Despite
months of therapy things get worse for

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:52.049
both Mr. and Mrs. Martin. Together they
go to the hospital where Mr. Martin's

00:01:52.049 --> 00:01:57.210
doctor prescribes painkillers. Mrs.
Martin decides to get a second opinion.

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:02.670
Her new doctor has recently learned that
for some chronic pain placebos work

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:06.780
equally well. Instead of giving Mrs.
Martin painkillers

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.250
the doctor prescribes simple sugar pills
though he tells Mrs. Martin that they

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:15.239
are pain killers.
The next day they both feel much better.

00:02:15.239 --> 00:02:20.650
Mr. Martin notices that he has no
problem sawing wood and Mrs. Martin can

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:26.230
easily put on her shoes. She can confirm
that the painkillers work but do they

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:33.010
really? Unfortunately, it doesn't take
long before the pain comes back and they

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:36.580
return to the hospital.
Mr. Martin is now treated with

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:41.079
vertebroplasty, a popular treatment
offered to people who suffer from back

00:02:41.079 --> 00:02:47.140
pain due to osteoporosis. To administer
it the doctors inject cement directly

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:52.660
into his vertebrae, the bones that form
the spinal column. Mrs. Martin's doctor

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:57.579
simply has her smell a container full of
cement and then administers a saline

00:02:57.579 --> 00:03:03.489
injection, which does nothing.
Her doctor learned about this placebo

00:03:03.489 --> 00:03:08.140
from research published in the U.S.
National Library of Medicine. It showed

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:13.660
that a large randomized controlled trial
found no benefit of vertebroplasty over

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:18.849
a sham procedure. Right after the surgery
the Martin's meet in the lobby and share

00:03:18.849 --> 00:03:24.160
their experience of the process: both
feel great! Mrs. Martin invites her

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:29.139
husband for ice cream as her treatment
was so much cheaper. So what's happening

00:03:29.139 --> 00:03:36.459
here? There are a couple of theories that
try to explain the placebo effect. First

00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:41.799
there is regression to the mean: Mr.
Martin like most of us thinks about

00:03:41.799 --> 00:03:46.269
treatment when his symptoms are
particularly bad. He goes to see a doctor

00:03:46.269 --> 00:03:51.250
and soon after feels better. If we look
at the natural course of many illnesses

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:57.730
we understand that pain, over time, comes
and goes in swings and usually regresses

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:02.889
to the mean. We don't know if the doctor
or placebo had anything to do with the

00:04:02.889 --> 00:04:07.959
improvement.
Then there is classical conditioning:

00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:13.700
most treatments, including vertebroplasty,
are delivered in a context of rituals

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:19.970
that include social signals, physical
cues, and verbal suggestions. Mr. Martin's

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:26.270
brain interprets such cues and elicits
expectations memories and emotions, it

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:31.160
releases endorphins and other chemicals
that make him feel good and lower his

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:36.320
perception of pain. So it becomes a
self-fulfilling prophecy where a belief

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:43.970
that he feels better leads him to feel
better. And there is confirmation bias: as

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:49.610
soon as Mrs. Martin takes the sugar pill
she thinks she will feel better. Then she

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:54.530
focuses only on the things that confirm
that she is better. She doesn't realize

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:58.055
that she still has trouble doing many
other things. While all three ideas

00:04:59.479 --> 00:05:05.750
probably work together there is another 
theory: so-called mirror neurons might

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:11.360
also play a role. A new and growing body
of evidence points at brain cells that

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:16.909
mirror behavior. The cells fire when one
acts and when one observes the same

00:05:16.909 --> 00:05:22.130
action performed by another. As Mrs.
Martin talks to the doctor parts of the

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:26.630
doctors brain will mirror parts of her
brain and parts of her brain will mirror

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:32.419
his, as a result, the structure of her
brain changes and she feels less pain.

00:05:32.419 --> 00:05:38.690
The neurophysiologist Giacomo Rizzolatti
who discovered mirror neurons suggests

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:44.000
that this process bypasses consciousness
and provides a direct mapping of sensory

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.099
information onto motor structures.

00:05:48.199 --> 00:05:53.759
Placebo, a Latin word that means "I will
please", have been used for thousands of

00:05:53.759 --> 00:05:58.770
years. Placebo effects have been
discussed for centuries. An influential

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:05.250
study from 1955 by Henry Kay Beecher,
Harvard, titled: the powerful placebo

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:10.800
established the idea that the effect is
clinically important. Today the placebo

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:15.389
effect is well recognized and
scientifically so significant that any

00:06:15.389 --> 00:06:19.770
new pain medication that seeks Food and
Drug Administration approval in the

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:26.690
United States needs to show that it
works better than a placebo treatment. In

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:31.680
so-called randomized controlled trials,
the gold standard of medical research,

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:37.110
one group of patients is given the new
medication while a control group receives

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:40.590
a placebo.
Neither the doctors who hand out the

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:46.650
medication nor the patients know who
gets what. Once the trial is over results

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:51.960
are compared. If the new medication works
significantly better than the placebo it's

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:57.509
allowed to be sold. The trial is
surprisingly difficult from 10 new drugs

00:06:57.509 --> 00:07:03.270
entering the test one gets approval. If a
placebo study proves that an existing

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:07.050
standard medical procedure is
ineffective, like in the case of

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:12.240
vertebroplasty, competent doctors stop
prescribing it and we can speak of

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:18.750
medical reversal. To find out if an
existing treatment works or if it's

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:22.830
healing power is just the result of the
placebo effect we can administer

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:27.870
treatment without the knowledge of the
patients. In one such experiment it was

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:31.740
shown that if a painkiller is
administered by a hidden robot pump,

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:36.449
patients demanded twice the dose
compared to when the drug is injected by

00:07:36.449 --> 00:07:40.800
a nurse. This would suggest that if a
patient is completely unaware that

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:46.080
treatment is being given, the treatment
is just half as effective. The placebo

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:52.719
effect counts for the other half.
Honest placebo studies go even further.

00:07:52.719 --> 00:07:57.279
Because deception is ethically
questionable researchers have now

00:07:57.279 --> 00:08:01.719
started to do clinical trials in which
people are told that all they get is a

00:08:01.719 --> 00:08:07.329
sugar pill with placebo printed all over
the packaging. And even then the placebo

00:08:07.329 --> 00:08:10.689
effect does it's magic and helps you
feel better.

00:08:10.689 --> 00:08:15.159
One experiment at the Harvard Medical
School showed that people suffering from

00:08:15.159 --> 00:08:20.139
irritable bowel syndrome who were taking
the honest placebo doubled their rate of

00:08:20.139 --> 00:08:26.319
improvement compared to the control
group. What do you think? How can we make

00:08:26.319 --> 00:08:30.369
sure that the medicine we are
prescribing is not only effective thanks

00:08:30.369 --> 00:08:35.469
to the placebo effect? Will more placebo
research reveal that many standard

00:08:35.469 --> 00:08:39.459
medical treatments offered in some of
the best hospitals around the world are

00:08:39.459 --> 00:08:45.220
shams? And how can we research the power
of placeboes ourselves, at home, without

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:51.600
putting anyone in danger?

